:"For large forms, split rendering into functions typed with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"LitFormType"},{"type":"text","value":", use a\nscoped "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.formGroup(...)"},{"type":"text","value":", or build reusable virtual field bundles with\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"getFieldGroupHelpers()"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of casting each field value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"form-state-changed-but-the-template-did-not-update","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Form state changed but the template did not update"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Render field state inside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.field(...)"},{"type":"text","value":" and selected form state inside\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.subscribe(...)"},{"type":"text","value":". These Lit directives update only their own child parts.\nReading "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"form.api.state"},{"type":"text","value":" directly in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"render()"},{"type":"text","value":" does not subscribe that markup\nto later changes."}]},{"type":"code","value":"this.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => state.isSubmitting,\n  (isSubmitting) => html` <button ?disabled=${isSubmitting}>Submit</button> `,\n)","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Both directives must be interpolated into a Lit child part. They cannot be used\nas attribute directives."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type instantiation is excessively deep"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported generic wrapper. Reduce it to the\nsmallest form that reproduces the problem, keep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"defaultValues"},{"type":"text","value":" concrete, and\navoid unnecessary generic layers."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n"},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TanStack Form issue tracker"}]},{"type":"text","value":". Include\nthe TypeScript version, form value type, and smallest failing field."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Errors exist but are not displayed"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" respects the form's "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"errorVisibility"},{"type":"text","value":" policy. Inspect\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.meta.original.errors"},{"type":"text","value":" to determine whether validation ran but the issues\nwere intentionally hidden. Confirm that the input calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"field.handleBlur()"},{"type":"text","value":" if\nthe policy depends on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"isBlurred"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"an-input-renders-an-empty-or-undefined-value","text":"An input renders an empty or undefined value","level":2},{"id":"a-field-value-is-unknown","text":"A field value is unknown","level":2},{"id":"form-state-changed-but-the-template-did-not-update","text":"Form state changed but the template did not update","level":2},{"id":"type-instantiation-is-excessively-deep","text":"Type instantiation is excessively deep","level":2},{"id":"errors-exist-but-are-not-displayed","text":"Errors exist but are not displayed","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nThis page covers common Lit and TypeScript problems when using TanStack Form.\n\n## An input renders an empty or undefined value\n\nEvery value bound to an input must exist in form-level `defaultValues` from the\nfirst render.\n\n```ts\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before creating the editable controller or\nprovide a complete fallback shape and call `form.update(...)` when data arrives.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that the\ninitial object has not been widened to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```ts\ntype Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nconst form = new TanStackFormController(this, { defaultValues: defaults })\n```\n\nFor large forms, split rendering into functions typed with `LitFormType`, use a\nscoped `form.formGroup(...)`, or build reusable virtual field bundles with\n`getFieldGroupHelpers()` instead of casting each field value.\n\n## Form state changed but the template did not update\n\nRender field state inside `form.field(...)` and selected form state inside\n`form.subscribe(...)`. These Lit directives update only their own child parts.\nReading `form.api.state` directly in `render()` does not subscribe that markup\nto later changes.\n\n```ts\nthis.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => state.isSubmitting,\n  (isSubmitting) => html` <button ?disabled=${isSubmitting}>Submit</button> `,\n)\n```\n\nBoth directives must be interpolated into a Lit child part. They cannot be used\nas attribute directives.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported generic wrapper. Reduce it to the\nsmallest form that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and\navoid unnecessary generic layers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe TypeScript version, form value type, and smallest failing field.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.meta.original.errors` to determine whether validation ran but the issues\nwere intentionally hidden. Confirm that the input calls `field.handleBlur()` if\nthe policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: debugging\ntitle: Debugging Lit Usage\n---\n\nThis page covers common Lit and TypeScript problems when using TanStack Form.\n\n## An input renders an empty or undefined value\n\nEvery value bound to an input must exist in form-level `defaultValues` from the\nfirst render.\n\n```ts\nprivate form = new TanStackFormController(this, {\n  defaultValues: {\n    firstName: '',\n    subscribed: false,\n  },\n})\n```\n\nDo not omit `defaultValues` or rely on a field-level default. When values come\nfrom an API, render a loading state before creating the editable controller or\nprovide a complete fallback shape and call `form.update(...)` when data arrives.\n\n## A field value is `unknown`\n\nField names and values are inferred from `defaultValues`. Check that the\ninitial object has not been widened to `Record<string, unknown>`, `any`, or an\nunrelated union. Prefer a concrete value type:\n\n```ts\ntype Profile = { firstName: string; age: number }\n\nconst defaults: Profile = { firstName: '', age: 0 }\nconst form = new TanStackFormController(this, { defaultValues: defaults })\n```\n\nFor large forms, split rendering into functions typed with `LitFormType`, use a\nscoped `form.formGroup(...)`, or build reusable virtual field bundles with\n`getFieldGroupHelpers()` instead of casting each field value.\n\n## Form state changed but the template did not update\n\nRender field state inside `form.field(...)` and selected form state inside\n`form.subscribe(...)`. These Lit directives update only their own child parts.\nReading `form.api.state` directly in `render()` does not subscribe that markup\nto later changes.\n\n```ts\nthis.form.subscribe(\n  (state) => state.isSubmitting,\n  (isSubmitting) => html` <button ?disabled=${isSubmitting}>Submit</button> `,\n)\n```\n\nBoth directives must be interpolated into a Lit child part. They cannot be used\nas attribute directives.\n\n## Type instantiation is excessively deep\n\nThis TypeScript error usually involves a very large recursive value shape, a\nwidely inferred union, or an unsupported generic wrapper. Reduce it to the\nsmallest form that reproduces the problem, keep `defaultValues` concrete, and\navoid unnecessary generic layers.\n\nIf the minimal reproduction still fails, report it in the\n[TanStack Form issue tracker](https://github.com/TanStack/form/issues). Include\nthe TypeScript version, form value type, and smallest failing field.\n\n## Errors exist but are not displayed\n\n`field.errors` respects the form's `errorVisibility` policy. Inspect\n`field.meta.original.errors` to determine whether validation ran but the issues\nwere intentionally hidden. Confirm that the input calls `field.handleBlur()` if\nthe policy depends on `isBlurred`.\n"}
